{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-switch-phone-components-1-a-01","date":"2026-11-26","lens":"gap-1","surface":"phone","area":"phone/components-1","refs":["F-phone-1315"],"severity":"S3","title":"The Charts page Balance check ignores the Muscle tips switch and the muscles a member put away","what":"A member who turns Muscle tips off in Settings, or says 'I skip this on purpose' or 'Not now' about a muscle on the Up next tip, still sees the Charts page Balance check name that same muscle as trained too little. Pressing 'Not now' on the Balance check does not quiet the Up next tip either. The two keep separate lists and neither reads the other.","expected":"One answer from the member about a muscle (off, skip on purpose, not now) quiets both places that give muscle advice, or the Settings page says the Charts card is separate.","evidence":["apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/balanceCheck.ts:84-86","apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/balanceCheck.ts:37-50","apps/mobile/src/tracker/store/muscleTipsStore.ts:2-5","apps/mobile/src/tracker/store/muscleTipsStore.ts:43-47","apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/muscleTips.ts:63","apps/mobile/src/components/analytics/BalanceCard.tsx:35-45"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"two-muscle-advice-quiet-lists","who":"members with 4+ weeks of workouts","how_often":"every Charts visit after a member put a muscle away","fix_line":"Make the Balance check skip muscles the member turned off or put away in Muscle tips, and share one Not now","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-switch-phone-components-1-a-02","date":"2026-11-26","lens":"gap-1","surface":"phone","area":"phone/components-1","refs":["F-phone-1313"],"severity":"S4","title":"What's new talks in kilos to members who chose pounds","what":"The 'New in this version' card and earlier updates are fixed text that says 'kilos you lifted' and 'kg lifted'. A member who set Units to pounds reads kilos here while every chart and workout screen shows pounds.","expected":"What's new lines follow the member's Units choice, or use unit-free words like 'weight lifted'.","evidence":["apps/mobile/src/lib/whatsNew.ts:125","apps/mobile/src/lib/whatsNew.ts:175","apps/mobile/src/components/WhatsNewList.tsx:33","apps/mobile/src/components/analytics/VolumeSection.tsx:18"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"whats-new-ignores-units-setting","who":"members who use pounds","how_often":"each new version","fix_line":"Write those lines without a unit, or fill in the member's unit when drawing them","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
